{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "The Secret Valentine", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Shopping With Sally", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 1, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 13, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B1.3", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Describe events through a wider range of B1 language in both work and social contexts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn8le13ob01re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Inseparable Phrasal Verbs", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " Phrasal verbs are two-part verbs consisting of a verb followed by an adverb particle (these look like prepositions, but do not have the same function in phrasal verbs). <br /> In some cases, it is not possible to separate the verb and the particle. These are called <span class=\"italic\">inseparable</span> phrasal verbs.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "It is important to remember that the meaning of a phrasal verb is often very different from the two parts taken separately. <br />For example:<br />  Be careful not to <span class=\"strong\">slip up</span> like you did last time (<span class=\"italic\">slip</span> is not the same as <span class=\"italic\">slip + up</span>). <br /><br /> <span class=\"italic\">To slip up </span>is an inseparable phrasal verb. You cannot put an object between the verb and the particle. It must remain together.  Another example is <span class=\"italic\">to tear into</span>. <br /> You can say \"<span class=\"strong\">tear into</span> someone\", but you cannot say \"<span class=\"strong\">tear</span> me <span class=\"strong\">into</span>\". <br /><br /> A few verbs can be used with both a particle and a preposition, making them <span class=\"strong\">three-part verbs</span>. <br />For example:<br /> <span class=\"italic\">to go on about </span>(to continue talking) <br /><br /> Learning phrasal verbs is a lot like learning new vocabulary. You must memorize which phrasal verbs are inseparable and learn their meanings.  <br /><br /> Look at the chart for some more inseparable phrasal verbs and their meanings.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":6,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Phrasal Verb\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Meaning\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" slip up\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" to make a mistake\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" go on about\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" to continue talking for a long time\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" tear into\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" to criticize harshly\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" meet up with\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" to meet\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" dress up\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" to dress smartly or formally\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "Just be careful not to <span class=\"strong\">slip up </span>like you did last time!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "She <span class=\"strong\">went on about</span> how badly people behave because of technology.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Last time she <span class=\"strong\">tore into</span> me about being single. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Your aunt will <span class=\"strong\">brighten up</span> when she sees how smashing you look.", "type": "example"}, {"content": " I'm supposed to <span class=\"strong\">meet up</span> with my eccentric old aunt for dinner tonight.", "type": "example"}, {"content": " <span class=\"prelo-letter-page-break\"></span>", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " Modals for Suggestion, Necessity, and Possibility", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " Modals are auxiliary verbs that function in different ways. Modals  can offer suggestion, express necessity and show possibility. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You use modals to talk about degrees of certainty, possibility and necessity.<br /><br /> You use them to describe what is definite, probable, possible, or impossible from the speaker's point of view. <br /><br /> Modals are used with the base form of the main verb. <br /><br /> <span class=\"italic\">Should</span>(modal) + <span class=\"italic\">go</span>(main verb)<br /> You can think of modals as \"helping verbs\". They add meaning to the main verb of a sentence.  <br /><br /> Modals talking about <span class=\"strong\">suggestions</span> are:<br /> could, can and should. <br /><br />  <span class=\"italic\">We <span class=\"strong\">should find </span>you something elegant!</span><br /> <span class=\"italic\">I <span class=\"strong\">could borrow </span>your long-sleeved silk dress.</span> <br /><br />  Modals talking about <span class=\"strong\">necessity </span>are:<br /> must, have to, had better and ought to. <br /><br />  <span class=\"italic\">You <span class=\"strong\">have to try not to get too worked up </span>if she is critical. <br />You really <span class=\"strong\">must try</span> this cashmere sweater on.</span> <br /><br />  Modals talking about <span class=\"strong\">possibility</span> are:<br /> could, may and might. <br /><br /> <span class=\"italic\">You <span class=\"strong\">might have</span> fun seeing your aunt.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You'd <span class=\"strong\">better </span>dress up! ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "We <span class=\"strong\">should find</span> you something elegant! You really <span class=\"strong\">must try </span>this cashmere sweater on.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "You <span class=\"strong\">might have </span>fun. You have to try not to <span class=\"strong\">get too worked up </span>if she is critical. ", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to go on about", "type": "name"}, {"content": " to talk too much about something ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Your aunt always goes on about people's behavior.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le13ob01aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": " These are words you hear for talking about feelings and reactions. ", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to tear into", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to verbally attack someone", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: She tore into me about being single. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le13ob01aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to get worked up ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to get irritated ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: My aunt gets me worked up when she talks about me being single. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le13ob01aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to brighten up", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to become happier or cheered up", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Your aunt will brighten up when she sees how smashing you look. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le13ob01aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "long-sleeved ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "having sleeves that reach to the wrist", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I don't like sleeveless dresses; I prefer long-sleeved dresses. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le13ob01aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "smashing", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a person that looks wonderful ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You look smashing in that dress. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le13ob01aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "eccentric ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "someone who has unconventional behavior", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: My aunt is very eccentric; she has very strange ideas about relationships. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le13ob01aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Imagine a friend needs some suggestions about where to shop for clothes in your city.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Choose three stores that your friend could shop at.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Write a short description (50 words) of each store and the style of clothing they contain.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Write the reasons you think your friend should shop there (good quality, wide variety etc.).", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Read your descriptions aloud.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I suggest three stores to shop at.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I write a description of each store.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I explain why a friend should shop there.", "type": "text"}]}], "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"_data": [], "type": "welcome", "contents": [{}], "id": 0, "template_override": 1}, {"id": 1, "contents": [{"value": {"audiosrc": "engenn8le13ob01re2aud01", "images": [{"image": "engenn8le13ob01re2img05.jpg", "id": 0, "text": "", "time": "0"}, {"image": "engenn8le13ob01re2img05.jpg", "id": 1, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Wow! Sally, you must be feeling exhausted after last night's party!\n<br /><span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: Yes, and I'm supposed to meet up with my eccentric old aunt for dinner tonight at your restaurant!\n<br /><span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Then, you'd better dress up! We should find you something elegant!\n<br /><span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>:  Or maybe I could borrow your long-sleeved silk dress?", "time": "100"}, {"image": "engenn8le13ob01re2img01.jpg", "id": 2, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Let's look a little more first. I wonder what your aunt is all fired up about this time.\n<br /><span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: Last time she went on about how badly people behave because of technology.\n<br /><span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Poor Scarlett, she must be lonely.\n<br /><span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: I know she must be pretty sad living without her husband. Though he was her fourth!", "time": "18500"}, {"image": "engenn8le13ob01re2img05.jpg", "id": 3, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Just be careful not to slip up like you did last time!\n<br /><span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: Don't worry I definitely won't. Last time she tore into me about being single. She said, \"You should realize, my dear, that proper women get married!\"\n<br /><span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>:  That's almost funny. She must be shocked by how different our lives are from hers. You really must try this cashmere sweater on.\n<br /><span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: Yes that would go well with my black pencil skirt.", "time": "36300"}, {"image": "engenn8le13ob01re2img05.jpg", "id": 4, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: We found you an outfit! Your aunt will brighten up when she sees how smashing you look. You have to try not to get too worked up if she is critical.\n<br /><span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: I'm pretty apprehensive about seeing her.\n<br /><span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: You must be nervous! Still, you might have fun. You always have some wonderful stories to tell.\n<br /><span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: I'll tell you all about it.", "time": "63000"}], "coverimg": "engenn8le13ob01re2img05.jpg"}, "type": "slideshow"}], "template_override": 1, "_data": [], "type": "audio", "title": ""}], "exercises": [{"id": 0, "template_override": 1, "stimuli_ids": [0], "img_path": "", "type": "WLC", "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"content": "I can talk about clothing, socializing and going out. ", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "I can express suggestions, necessity and possibility.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "I can show I understand someone's feelings or situation. ", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "When you go shopping for clothes do you prefer being alone or having someone with you?", "type": "Free Header Item"}, {"content": "What kinds of clothes do you like buying?", "type": "Free Header Item"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"content": "Welcome", "type": "group_name"}]}, {"content": {"correct_feedback": "Correct", "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "try again", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time", "type": "text"}], "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "You have 2 tries", "type": "text"}, {"content": "you have 1 attempt left", "type": "text"}], "allowed_attempts": 2}, "type": "feedback"}, {"content": " Ask your partner:", "type": "free_header_text"}, {"content": " Shopping can be fun or tiring!", "type": "free_type_text_area"}], "questions": []}, {"id": 1, "template_override": 1, "stimuli_ids": [1], "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"content": " \nSally and Vanessa find an <span class=\"tool-tip\" id=\"tip_1_0\">elegant</span> outfit!\n", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"content": "Content", "type": "group_name"}]}, {"content": {"correct_feedback": "Correct!", "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "Whoops! Something important is missing.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time...", "type": "text"}], "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}, {"content": "", "type": "text"}], "allowed_attempts": 2}, "type": "feedback"}, {"type": "learning_skills", "contents": [{"content": "Reading", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "Listening", "type": "skill"}]}, {"content": [{"content": "<span class=\"italic\">\"Elegant\"</s